<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mthethwa Paramountcy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 18th century–c. 1818</span> · Also known as Mthethwa Empire</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mthethwa Paramountcy was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni</a> state near the coast of what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwazulu-natal">KwaZulu-Natal</a>, which under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingiswayo">Dingiswayo</a> dominated neighbouring chiefdoms, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a>, in the early 19th century. It competed with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndwandwe">Ndwandwe</a> for land, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delagoa-bay">Delagoa Bay</a> trade. After Dingiswayo's death around 1818 its followers were absorbed into Shaka's Zulu Kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mthethwa-paramountcy.jpg" alt="Mthethwa Paramountcy" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SFC9394 · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_Africa_topo_continent.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
